okf_version: "1.0"
task: "Session backup target for a Synology NAS reached by QuickConnect (File Station Web API), fully operable from menu 18."
requested: "User, 2026-10-10: '백업하는 방븝어로 Synology QC connect 지원' with the QuickConnect ID, account and password; after the plan: 'Synology QuickConnect을 이용한 백업기능 추가 승인'. The password was not written to any file, commit or log by me, and I did not type it anywhere."
research:
  official: "Synology File Station API Guide (PDF, global.download.synology.com .../Package/FileStation/...): workflow SYNO.API.Info query -> SYNO.API.Auth login (account, passwd, session, format=sid; codes 400 bad password, 401 disabled, 402 denied, 403 2-step code required, 404 2-step failed) -> calls with _sid -> logout. Upload v2: multipart, file part last, path, create_parents, overwrite=true/false (v3: overwrite/skip); Download v2 method=download path=[\"...\"]; List folder_path/offset/limit; Delete has a blocking 'delete' method."
  quickconnect: "Not in Synology's public docs. Method from the community library N4S4/synology-api (auth.py), checked live: POST https://global.quickconnect.to/Serv.php get_server_info (serverID=<the user's ID>) -> errno 0, control_host usc.quickconnect.to, relay_region us2, ddns <id>.synology.me, service port 5001, interface <lan-ip>; request_tunnel at the control host -> relay_region us2, pingpong_path /webman/pingpong.cgi?action=cors&quickconnect=true. https://<id>.us2.quickconnect.to answers pingpong and SYNO.API.Info (Auth max v7, FileStation.Upload v2-3, Download/List/Delete/CreateFolder v1-2). From this PC <lan-ip>:5001 and <id>.synology.me:5001 time out - only the relay works."
changes:
  module: "ciel_runtime_support/session_backup_synology.py: quickconnect_addresses (DDNS first, then relay), DsmClient (connect via API info probe, login by POST form so the password is not in a URL, call/upload/download/list_folder/delete, relogin once on 106/107/119, DSM error codes mapped to text), SynologyTarget (blobs index listed once for dedupe, uploads per chunk - no staging on the low C: disk), build_synology_target (address/account/path required; password only as password_file or ${ENV}; a literal password is refused), DPAPI store/load (CryptProtectData with an entropy, UI forbidden). TLS is always verified; plain http:// only when an address is given explicitly (used by the E2E stand-in)."
  wiring: "session_backup_targets: TARGET_TYPES + synology. session_backup_menu: Add a target… lists Synology QuickConnect; fields QuickConnect ID (or https://host:port), DSM account, NAS folder; the password prompt is hidden (prompt_menu_value secret) and stored with DPAPI in CONFIG_DIR/backup-credentials/<name>.dpapi, or taken as ${ENV}; target row actions use / test / password / remove (remove deletes the credential file); row detail 'synology · account@address:path · password stored'. prelaunch passes secret= through. session_backup_cli closes every remote target it built when a command ends (Synology logs out; SSH/rclone staging folders are removed - before, close() was never called by the CLI)."
tests: "tests/test_session_backup_synology.py 9 (relay fallback when DDNS is unreachable and Origin header + pingpong first; round trip / dedupe / list / delete / manifest JSON not mistaken for an error; wrong password and full NAS volume stop the backup via TargetWriteError; expired session logs in again once; literal password refused; DPAPI round trip without plaintext; menu add/test/password/remove with the hidden prompt; CLI create twice -> second uploads 0 chunks, restore, verify, all sessions logged out). Groups: unit 1826 OK, runtime 402 OK, channel 457 OK, router 1188 OK; ruff clean; router 9611 200."
e2e:
  harness: "evidence/e2e_synology_menu.py (+ _steps.py, console_driver.py, shot_hwnd.ps1): menu in conhost driven by key events; a DSM stand-in on 127.0.0.1 (plain HTTP) implementing the calls above; isolated config/home/work on G:; stand-in passwords made up for the test."
  result: "Run 14:48: Add a target… -> synology/nas-e2e/http://127.0.0.1:PORT/ciel-backup//backup/ciel, password typed (screen shows only the prompt), 'Added target nas-e2e (synology · ciel-backup@...:/backup/ciel · password stored)' + 'Test: write, read and delete worked.'; local switched off; Back up now -> 'Saved snapshot'; again -> 'incremental: 0 of 3 chunks new, 0.0 MB uploaded'; Verify -> 'complete, every chunk checks out'; notes.md changed then Restore -> 'Restored …' and notes.md back to 'plan v1'; stand-in password changed -> test 'NAS error 400: no such account or incorrect password' -> password action -> 'password stored for this Windows user' -> test worked. session-backup.json holds no password; the .dpapi file (246 bytes) holds no plaintext; stand-in calls: login 12 (one refused by design) / logout 11."
  real_nas: "Without credentials: DsmClient('<the user's ID>').connect() through the code -> https://<id>.us2.quickconnect.to in 9.8 s (about 8 s is the DDNS attempt timing out) and the full FileStation API list. A real login/backup needs the user to type the password into the menu (I do not enter passwords)."
real_nas_test:
  setup: "2026-10-10 19:05-19:46, the user's NAS over QuickConnect (only the relay answers from this PC), NAS folder /home/ciel-backup, isolated config/home on G:, work folder 72.4 MB (64 MB random, jsonl, 2 small files). The menu was driven by key events; the user typed the DSM password into the menu window (the agent does not enter passwords). Screens and logs stay on this PC only (they show the NAS ID and account; the repo is public): evidence/e2e-2-real-nas, excluded via .git/info/exclude."
  incidents: "Run 1: Git Bash turned the argument /home/ciel-backup into C:/Program Files/Git/home/ciel-backup - stopped before any password was typed, nothing saved, rerun with MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1. Run 2: the password prompt got an empty value ('Not added: no password given'; getpass read only Enter) - cause unknown (focus or IME suspected, unverified); run 3 worked."
  results: "Test: write, read and delete worked. First backup: 13 of 13 chunks, 64.0 MB uploaded in ~15 min (~70 KB/s) - the menu looked frozen: nothing changed on the progress line while chunks uploaded (fixed below). Incremental: 0 of 13 new, 29.8 s. Verify: complete, every chunk checks out, 86 s (72.4 MB read back, ~0.85 MB/s). Restore: 'Restored 5 files', safety snapshot taken, notes.md back to 'plan v1', 103.8 s. Snapshot list shown."
  speed: "backup create via the CLI with the stored credential: 8 MB in 4 chunks - jobs 1 40.5 s (202 KB/s), jobs 8 22.1 s (371 KB/s); after the probe fix, 32 MB in 8 chunks - jobs 8 19.9 s (1646 KB/s), jobs 1 65.5 s (500 KB/s). The slow first backup (~70 KB/s) is not explained by these numbers."
  fixes_after: "Progress during uploads: ChunkWriter.drain(report) calls the collector every second with phase 'uploading' (chunks still sending, stored MB, sent MB); the Synology client counts body bytes as http.client sends them (bytes_sent) so the line moves within a chunk; menu line 'Uploading: N chunk(s) still sending, X MB stored, Y MB sent (T s)'. Connect: all addresses are probed at once and the first answer wins - connect 9.8 s -> 1.8 s (the unreachable DDNS probe used to cost its 8 s timeout on every command; it may still finish in the background)."
  cleanup: "The test menu closed; G:\ciel-e2e\nas-real (with the DPAPI password file) deleted. Test snapshots remain on the NAS in /home/ciel-backup."
not_verified:
  - "Accounts with 2-step verification (the API refuses them with 403; the message says so)."
  - "Why the first real-NAS backup ran at ~70 KB/s while later uploads ran at 0.5-1.6 MB/s."
not_done: "Committed in 56b279a (target) and the next commit (progress, probe race)."
